\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The resolution floor and name-first economy} (\Cref  {sec:floor}). (A) Over $500$ random contact graphs, the distinction cost $\sigma (v)$ sits on or above the floor plane $z=\beta $ for every constituent---no point falls below. (B) The ratio $\sigma (v)/\beta $ is supported entirely at or above $1$ across $300$ graphs and $2511$ cut checks, with measured minimum $\sigma (v)/\beta =1.0010$ and \emph  {zero} cuts below the floor (\Cref  {thm:floor}). (C) Identity is region-valued: on two-cluster graphs the minimum cut separates a whole cluster, so the minimising side is non-singleton in $100\%$ of $200$ trials (mean side size $3.9$), confirming \Cref  {cor:no-point}. (D) Acoustic invocations equal the residual size exactly across streams of increasing unnamed fraction ($400/400$ trials, acoustic calls $=r$), realising \Cref  {cor:name-first}.}}{7}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:floor}{{1}{7}{\textbf {The resolution floor and name-first economy} (\Cref {sec:floor}). (A) Over $500$ random contact graphs, the distinction cost $\str (v)$ sits on or above the floor plane $z=\flo $ for every constituent---no point falls below. (B) The ratio $\str (v)/\flo $ is supported entirely at or above $1$ across $300$ graphs and $2511$ cut checks, with measured minimum $\str (v)/\flo =1.0010$ and \emph {zero} cuts below the floor (\Cref {thm:floor}). (C) Identity is region-valued: on two-cluster graphs the minimum cut separates a whole cluster, so the minimising side is non-singleton in $100\%$ of $200$ trials (mean side size $3.9$), confirming \Cref {cor:no-point}. (D) Acoustic invocations equal the residual size exactly across streams of increasing unnamed fraction ($400/400$ trials, acoustic calls $=r$), realising \Cref {cor:name-first}}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:floor@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][6][]7}{}{}{}}
